    },
    {
      "at": "0x68578e64",
      "finding": "GetPanelAttribute implementation case 0x250 (592 ATTR_CLOSE_CTRL) calls 0x68588d5a; returned associated control object ID is read at +0x28 in 0x68578f76. Setter case 0x250 resolves provided control ID then uses 0x68588ce2."
    },
    {
      "at": "0x68571144",
      "finding": "For unconsumed panel event 0x0b, valid panel, close-control object present, and dispatch enabled, calls 0x68588d5a and sends internal event 0x271c with control native handle +0xac and event argument 1 at 0x68571187."
    }
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Static analysis supports normal titlebar/system-menu Close (WM_SYSCOMMAND/SC_CLOSE). It does not establish arbitrary externally posted WM_CLOSE as equivalent; direct WM_CLOSE was not fully traced.",
    "Runtime gating exists: panel/native flags, valid panel/control handles, event loop state, event-consumption callback return, and dispatch mode can suppress handling. Runtime state was not inspected here.",
    "ATTR_CLOSE_CTRL=2 and control 2 callback QuitProgram -> QuitUserInterface(0) are facts supplied by parent, not independently re-derived in this DLL review.",
    "No process was closed, no remote action occurred, and no source or binary was modified."
